# Frontend Boundary

- The current focus is **backend**. Any frontend change requires explicit human approval first.
- When backend work changes an API contract the frontend depends on, document the change (in the task report and `docs/ai/CURRENT_STATE.md`) instead of patching the frontend.
- Do not create temporary frontend workarounds to make a backend change appear complete.

Known deferred frontend work (do not start without approval):

- Password-rotation UI (redirect on `mustChangePassword`, change-password screen).
- Explicit user selection for PIN login (`userId` + `pin` payload).
- Explicit manager selection for approvals (`managerUserId` + `managerPin` payload).
- Updated PIN request payloads replacing anonymous quick-login.
- Future SEC-02B manager approval UX (terminal/session-bound grants).
